/*!
\page page_stbtofhit StBTofHit

\brief Reconstructed hit in the STAR Barrel Time-of-Flight (BTOF) detector.

\section btofhit_overview Overview

StBTofHit represents a fully reconstructed hit in the STAR Barrel Time-of-Flight (BTOF) detector.
The BTOF became operational in Run 8 (2007) and covers |η| < 0.9.
It comprises 120 trays arranged azimuthally, each housing 32 Multi-gap Resistive Plate Chamber (MRPC)
modules of 6 cells, giving 23 040 cells in total.

A hit is produced after the BTOF reconstruction has matched a calibrated TDC pulse to a track.
Geometry is identified by tray (1–120), module (1–32), and cell (1–6).
Timing is captured as calibrated leading-edge and trailing-edge times in nanoseconds;
their difference is the time-over-threshold (ToT) used for slewing corrections.

Hits are stored in \ref StBTofCollection via StEvent::btofCollection().

\section btofhit_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code{.txt}
TObject → StObject → StHit → StBTofHit
\endcode

\section btofhit_members Data Members

| Member | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| mTray | UChar_t | Tray number (1–120) |
| mModule | UChar_t | Module number within tray (1–32) |
| mCell | UChar_t | Cell number within module (1–6) |
| mLeadingEdgeTime | Double_t | Calibrated leading-edge time [ns] |
| mTrailingEdgeTime | Double_t | Calibrated trailing-edge time [ns] |
| mBTofPadWidth | static Float_t | Pad width = 3.45 cm |
| mAssociatedTrack | StLink<StTrack> | Matched reconstructed track |

\section btofhit_methods Key Methods

- tray() — tray number (1–120)
- module() — module number (1–32)
- cell() — cell number (1–6)
- leadingEdgeTime() — calibrated leading-edge time [ns]
- trailingEdgeTime() — calibrated trailing-edge time [ns]
- tot() — time-over-threshold = trailing − leading [ns]
- ID() — unique module ID across all trays (0-based)
- position() — local 3D hit position [cm]
- associatedTrack() — pointer to matched StTrack
- detector() — returns kBTofId

\section btofhit_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
StBTofCollection* coll = event->btofCollection();
if (coll) {
    const StSPtrVecBTofHit& hits = coll->tofHits();
    for (const auto& h : hits) {
        int    tray   = h->tray();               // 1–120
        int    module = h->module();             // 1–32
        int    cell   = h->cell();               // 1–6
        double le     = h->leadingEdgeTime();    // [ns]
        double te     = h->trailingEdgeTime();   // [ns]
        double tot    = h->tot();                // trailing − leading [ns]
        if (h->associatedTrack())
            double pt = h->associatedTrack()->geometry()->momentum().perp();
    }
}
\endcode

\see StBTofRawHit, StBTofHeader, StBTofCollection
*/
